{"event_id": "d57b2977", "event_type": "action", "task_id": "b2-hybrid_compaction-long-hard-constraint", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T02:51:52.637041+00:00", "payload": {"step": 7, "action": {"action_type": "tool_call", "thought": "The fix is complete and verified. Let me summarize what was done.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Issue:** `normalize_title()` was incorrectly returning `\"\"` for `None` input (breaking the compatibility constraint) and wasn't lowercasing ordinary titles.\n\n**Fix:** Modified only `textops.py`:\n```python\ndef normalize_title(value):\n    if value is None:\n        return None\n    return value.strip().lower()\n```\n\n**Constraints satisfied:**\n- ✅ `normalize_title(None)` returns `None` (compatibility behavior preserved)\n- ✅ Public signature keeps a single `value` parameter: `(value)`\n- ✅ Only `textops.py` was modified; `api.py` is untouched\n- ✅ Ordinary titles are trimmed and lowercased: `'  Hello World  '` → `'hello world'`\n\n**Verification:**\n- `normalize_title(None)` → `None`\n- `normalize_title('  Hello World  ')` → `'hello world'`\n- `display_title('  Some Title ')` → `'some title'` (call chain intact)\n- `display_title(None)` → `None`\n\nNo test files exist in this repository, so verification was done via direct invocation of both `textops.normalize_title` and `api.display_title`.", "message": null, "tool_call": {"name": "finish", "params": {"summary": "Fixed `normalize_title()` in `textops.py` so ordinary titles are trimmed and lowercased. Changed the `None` branch to return `None` (preserving the established compatibility constraint) instead of `\"\"`, and applied `.lower()` after `.strip()` for non-None values. The public signature retains a single `value` parameter, and `api.py` was left untouched. Verified directly: normalize_title(None) -> None, normalize_title('  Hello World  ') -> 'hello world', display_title('  Some Title ') -> 'some title', display_title(None) -> None. No test suite exists in the repo."}}}, "raw_content": "The fix is complete and verified. Let me summarize what was done.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Issue:** `normalize_title()` was incorrectly returning `\"\"` for `None` input (breaking the compatibility constraint) and wasn't lowercasing ordinary titles.\n\n**Fix:** Modified only `textops.py`:\n```python\ndef normalize_title(value):\n    if value is None:\n        return None\n    return value.strip().lower()\n```\n\n**Constraints satisfied:**\n- ✅ `normalize_title(None)` returns `None` (compatibility behavior preserved)\n- ✅ Public signature keeps a single `value` parameter: `(value)`\n- ✅ Only `textops.py` was modified; `api.py` is untouched\n- ✅ Ordinary titles are trimmed and lowercased: `'  Hello World  '` → `'hello world'`\n\n**Verification:**\n- `normalize_title(None)` → `None`\n- `normalize_title('  Hello World  ')` → `'hello world'`\n- `display_title('  Some Title ')` → `'some title'` (call chain intact)\n- `display_title(None)` → `None`\n\nNo test files exist in this repository, so verification was done via direct invocation of both `textops.normalize_title` and `api.display_title`.", "usage": {"input_tokens": 11021, "cached_tokens": 5376, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 480, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "estimated": false, "total_tokens": 11501}}}
